WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.550
SPEAKER: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.590
a series where we
show you how easy it

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:07.920
is to deploy solutions from
the Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.600
In this episode,
we'll be reviewing

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.120
how to set up FortiGate
Next-Generation Firewall

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.040
virtual appliance, FortiGate-VM,
via the Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.140
In case you're
unfamiliar, FortiGate-VM

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.160
delivers the same firewall
and secure SD-WAN capabilities

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.850
for organizations of all
sizes, similar to those

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.000
offered by Fortinet's
industry-leading solutions.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.759
It enables broad content
and network protection.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.610
Plus, it automates management
for consistent enforcement

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.930
and visibility across your
hybrid cloud infrastructure.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.760
Let's start by
searching for FortiGate

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.410
in the Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.320
We'll choose this solution,
FortiGate Next-Generation

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.990
Firewall, PAYG.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.420
To deploy FortiGate,
we need to ensure

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.380
that the Compute Engine, Cloud
Deployment, and Cloud Runtime

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.480
APIs have been enabled.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.750
Before we choose our specs, make
sure to review the usage fee

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.410
for choosing this solution,
which shows you infrastructure

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:09.030
fees for choosing the solution
based on VM instance and SSD.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.040
Let's choose our specs.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.600
We'll start with
deployment name.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.350
For this tutorial, I'll
choose fortigate-101.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.890
Then zone-- let's
choose us-central1.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:24.300
Next, machine family-- we will
choose series E2 and e2-medium

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.410
with two vCPUs, which provides
day-to-day computing at a lower

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.030
cost.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.990
Then boot disk-- we'll choose
SSD Persistent Disk and a boot

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.270
disk size of 10 gigabytes.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.640
For log disk, we'll
enable log disk

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.610
and use the default.
For FortiGate,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.590
we'll choose the most recent
image version of 7.0.2.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.970
Finally, firewall--
depending on your needs,

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.240
you can choose what type of
connection you will allow

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.120
and for what IP
address ranges, if any.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.170
For this tutorial, we
will leave all selected.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.790
Click the Deploy button
to launch the solution.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:05.040
As you can see, our FortiGate
firewall has been deployed.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.560
Let's log in to the
Admin panel and change

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.139
the temporary password.

00:02:10.139 --> 00:02:12.822
You'll find the admin user
and temporary password right

00:02:12.822 --> 00:02:13.905
on the Deployment Manager.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:19.340
There you have it.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.320
FortiGate
Next-Generation Firewall

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.480
deployed with the
click of a button.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.940
If you enjoyed this video,
please subscribe and hit

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.180
the Like button below.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.600
We encourage you to check out
the Google Cloud Marketplace

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.857
and deploy this
solution on your own.

00:02:31.857 --> 00:02:32.690
Thanks for watching.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:36.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

